# Metro DI Wiring

## Injectable classes — `@Inject` on the class
```kotlin
@Inject
class VehiclesViewModel(...) : MviViewModel<...>(State())

@Inject
class VehicleRepositoryImpl(...) : VehicleRepository

@Inject
class VehicleMapper
```

## DefaultViewModelProvider — manual wiring hub
```kotlin
// Lazy repository (via FeatureRepositoryFactory)
private val vehicleRepository by lazy { featureRepositoryFactory.vehicleRepository }

// Lazy use case (built from repository)
private val getVehiclesUseCase by lazy { GetVehiclesUseCase(vehicleRepository) }

// ViewModel factory method
override fun vehiclesViewModel(): VehiclesViewModel {
    return VehiclesViewModel(dispatcherProvider, getVehiclesUseCase, deleteVehicleUseCase)
}
```

## Adding a new feature to DI
1. Create repository impl in feature module
2. Add repository property in `FeatureRepositoryFactory`
3. Add use case lazy properties in `DefaultViewModelProvider`
4. Add ViewModel factory method to `ViewModelProvider` interface
5. Implement factory method in `DefaultViewModelProvider`
